    "recommendations": "• Mark the main driveway entrance with reflective address numbers visible from both directions of approach.\n• Mark each detached structure with a visible identifier so responders can communicate locations clearly during an incident.\n• Keep all access drive surfaces clear of parked equipment and vehicles to allow emergency vehicles to reach the rear of the property.\n• Identify and mark any secondary access points so responding crews can quickly determine available entry routes.\n• Keep gates serving the rear of the property unlocked or equipped with a rapid-release mechanism for emergency access.\n• Clear a path wide enough for a responder on foot to move between each detached structure without obstruction.\n• Designate and mark a flat, open staging area near the main access drive where emergency vehicles can park without blocking the drive.\n• Keep the equipment storage area organized so that stored equipment does not block movement between structures or toward the open terrain."
