    "recommendations": "• Move wood piles away from the house and any other structures, keeping them stored at a distance where flames could not reach the walls or roof.\n• Trim shrubs that are growing close to the house to increase the open space between the plants and the structure.\n• Remove dead or dry material from scattered shrubs near any outbuildings or fenced areas.\n• Keep the area directly around wood pile storage clear of dry leaves, twigs, and loose plant debris.\n• Thin scattered trees near the house so their branches do not touch or hang over the roof or walls.\n• Maintain open spacing between individual shrubs so fire cannot move easily from one plant to the next toward the structure.\n• Keep all access routes clear of overhanging branches and encroaching shrubs so vehicles can pass through without obstruction."
